      "writtenOn": "2022-05-10T07:47:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "updateConnectedClients (and ConnectedClientsTracker) assume that they are passed in the full list of all clients every time. But now this isn\u0027t obvious, since each callback would only pass in the clients that are respectively on normal and local-only softAp right ?\n\nI think this would cause all wifi clients to be considered disconnected when the local only hotspot callback is fired, and vice-versa. But from what I read in the bug, it\u0027s not possible to have local-only and hotspot enabled at the same time ?\n\nWhere is that enforced ? I think you should at least mention it in a comment, and at the place where that is enforced, mention that onConnectedClientsChanged should be updated if it is made possible to enable both simultaneously.\n\nIf it is not strictly enforced by Tethering, it\u0027s possible OEMs have actually implemented it, so this should be either forbidden or supported and tested.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 558,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 558,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "597319217ed8c2e814fe4ead443ff2be21ee6e9d",
