      "writtenOn": "2022-05-10T07:47:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"updateMacOnlyWifiTetheringClient\" and \"updateTetheredClients\" have similar naming, but they do very different things: the first one sends the wifi L2 change callback, the second one sends the onLeasesChanged callback.\n\n\"updateMacOnlyWifiTetheringClient\" also suggests that this is for a special type of wifi client that \"only has mac\", but actually all wifi clients should be in the same situation here.\n\nI\u0027d suggest naming closer to the callback that is being called, like \"notifyConnectedWifiClientsChanged\" and \"notifyDhcpLeasesChanged\"; even if the methods return TetheredClients (which is already self-explanatory when looking at the call), the \"action\" they do is to call the callback.",
